    "mapping_notes": "# flash_attention__fwd_hd256_bf16_2cta__sm_100a\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in source_interface.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Q | bf16 | 1 x 1 x 256 x 256 | input | Q |\n| K | bf16 | 1 x 1 x 256 x 256 | input | K |\n| V | bf16 | 1 x 1 x 256 x 256 | input | V |\n| O | bf16 | 1 x 1 x 256 x 256 | output | O |\n| scale_log2 | float | 0.09016844005556021 | input | scale_log2 |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nQ[b,h,q,d], K[b,kh,k,d], and V[b,kh,k,v] are the logical tensors.\nkh = floor(h / (query_heads / kv_heads)).\nscore[k] = scale_log2 * sum_d Q[b,h,q,d] * K[b,kh,k,d].\nO = sum_k 2^(score[k]-max(score)) * V[k] / sum_k 2^(score[k]-max(score)).\nThe selected FP8 example has no Q/K/V descale tensors; no extra scale is invented.\nQ descriptor coordinates are [d,q,0,h,b]; K and V use [d,k,h,b].\nO uses the source's direct output pointer. The configured output scale is one.\nThe selected entry has no LSE output pointer, so the reference does not invent one.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nNot compared against an optimized GPU execution.\nPrecision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/ce088ab9ce0fc0434dcd8afa0a791da9fcc3a820/flash_attn/cute/sm100_hd256_2cta_fmha_forward.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/ce088ab9ce0fc0434dcd8afa0a791da9fcc3a820/flash_attn/cute/interface.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/ce088ab9ce0fc0434dcd8afa0a791da9fcc3a820/flash_attn/cute/tile_scheduler.py\n"
